Error: apprafter::target::invalid_config

  × target config at <SANDBOX>/apprafter-config/targets/prod/
  │ credentials.yaml: not a valid target credentials map (line 1, column 1)
  help: <SANDBOX>/apprafter-config/targets/prod/credentials.yaml could
        not be read as target `prod`'s configuration: it was edited by hand or
        written by an incompatible CLI version. Fix it by hand (it is a small
        YAML file), or restore it from a backup. Otherwise remove the target
        with `apprafter target remove prod`, which takes a target it cannot
        read, and add it again with `apprafter target add prod --provider
        hetzner-cloud …`, its token too. The removal also deletes the target's
        local state: the record of its server, the cached kubeconfig and the
        Argo CD password. If a server is recorded, fix or restore the file
        first. After adding the target again, `apprafter import --target prod`
        rebuilds the record from the provider; the kubeconfig and the password
        are fetched again on first use.

